window.NEWS_DATA.en = {"three":[{"t":"Nvidia, the AI chip maker, suddenly loses its leader; NY stocks fall","x":"Nvidia of the US, the world's biggest maker of chips for AI, announced that CEO Huang, who led the company for more than 30 years, has resigned. Its finance chief, Ms. Kress, will be the temporary leader. He left while reports about his private life continued, and the stock fell more than 14% at one point (Nikkei, Reuters, NHK, CBS). On the 12th, the NY Dow fell 189 dollars (Kyodo, Jiji). The Houthis in Yemen said they attacked oil facilities in Saudi Arabia, and NY oil rose to the 88-dollar level (Kyodo, Al Jazeera). This is linked to Japanese chip stocks and to gasoline and electricity costs."},{"t":"The yen nears 160 to the dollar; the Ministry of Finance says it is moving too fast","x":"On the 12th, the yen was sold in Tokyo, and at 5 p.m. it was 159.71-159.72 yen to the dollar. In London it reached 160 yen for a while (Jiji, Yomiuri, Nikkei). Vice Finance Minister Mimura said the moves are too fast and suggested Japan could buy yen in the market (TV Tokyo, ANN, Kyodo, Reuters). The bill to cut the consumption tax on food will be discussed in a special committee of the House of Councillors from today, the 13th. Prime Minister Takaichi will also attend (NHK, ANN, Sankei, Kyodo). A weak yen makes imported goods more expensive, and the tax cut is linked to daily shopping. On the 12th, three parties sent a bill to Diet to cut 31 seats in the House of Representatives from proportional representation (NHK, Kyodo)."},{"t":"Winter electricity and gas bills will be about 7,000 yen cheaper over three months; decision today","x":"Today, the 13th, the cabinet will decide to use more than 651.8 billion yen from reserve funds for help with winter electricity and gas bills and for people who use kerosene. A normal household is expected to save about 7,000 yen over the three months from December to February (ANN, Kyodo, NHK). At the Asia professional baseball games at Tokyo Dome, Australia narrowly beat South Korea (NTV, Nikkan, Daily). Ohtani's National League MVP will be announced this morning, Japan time. Information also leaked from the Cabinet Office's email newsletter and SMBC Nikko Securities (announced on the 11th; Nikkei, NHK, Jiji)."}],"top10":[{"t":"Nvidia, the AI chip maker, loses its leader; stock falls 14% at one point","x":"New: Nvidia of the US, the world's biggest maker of chips for AI, announced that CEO Jensen Huang, who led the company for more than 30 years since it started, has resigned. Its finance chief, Colette Kress, will be the temporary leader (Nikkei, Reuters, NHK, CBS, CNN). He left while reports about his private life continued, and the stock fell about 14% at one point from its close on the 11th (NHK, Jiji). Nvidia will announce its results on the 17th. New: NY stocks fell on the 12th, and the Dow lost 189 dollars. AI-related stocks were sold (Kyodo, Jiji). People are watching chip stocks in Tokyo today too.","w":[["resign","辞任する"],["temporary","暫定の"]]},{"t":"Will imported goods cost more? The yen nears 160 and oil rises","x":"New: On the 12th, the yen was sold in Tokyo, and at 5 p.m. it was 159.71-159.72 yen to the dollar, more than 80 sen weaker than the day before (Jiji, Yomiuri). In London it reached 160 yen for a while (Nikkei). Vice Finance Minister Mimura said the moves are too fast and suggested Japan could buy yen in the market (TV Tokyo, ANN, Kyodo, Reuters). New: NY oil rose 2.55% on the 12th and closed at the 88-dollar level, after the Houthis in Yemen said they attacked oil facilities in Saudi Arabia (Kyodo, Minkabu). New: Today the cabinet will decide to use more than 651.8 billion yen from reserve funds for help with winter electricity and gas bills. A normal household is expected to save about 7,000 yen over three months (ANN, Kyodo, NHK).","w":[["weak yen","円安"],["import","輸入する"]]},{"t":"Putin's meeting with US envoys ends; Saudi oil facilities attacked in the Middle East","x":"New: The meeting between Russian President Putin and US envoys Witkoff and Kushner ended between the night of the 12th and this morning, Japan time (Kyodo, TIME, CNN). ANN reported that Putin showed understanding for new talks on European security, on the condition that NATO does not grow. The US side will next meet President Zelensky. New: In the Middle East, the Houthis in Yemen said on the 12th that they attacked pump facilities of Saudi Arabia's East-West oil pipeline and Yanbu on the Red Sea (Kyodo, Al Jazeera, The New Arab; the damage has not been confirmed). President Trump reportedly spoke negatively about a deal with Iran (The New Arab, Minkabu). Before this: The three-way talks among the US, Russia and Ukraine were held in Abu Dhabi on the 10th and 11th. They agreed on the largest release of prisoners and are making final arrangements (Kyodo, Jiji, Mainichi). There was no big progress such as a ceasefire (CNN, Anadolu, Kyodo). Iran's Revolutionary Guards said two oil tankers exploded and could not move on the night of the 11th (AFP, Xinhua; Iran's claim).","w":[["envoy","特使"],["pipeline","パイプライン"]]},{"t":"The food consumption tax cut is discussed in an upper house committee from today; the prime minister attends","x":"New: The bill to cut the consumption tax on food will be discussed in a special committee of the House of Councillors from today, the 13th, and Prime Minister Takaichi will attend. The ruling parties are two seats short of a majority in the upper house, so the focus is whether the Democratic Party for the People and Komeito will support it (NHK, ANN, Sankei, Kyodo). On the 12th, the LDP, Ishin and DPFP sent a bill to cut 31 proportional seats in the House of Representatives (NHK, Kyodo). LDP Vice President Aso criticized former Prime Minister Ishiba and others who left during the vote (Jiji, Mainichi, Sankei).","w":[["committee","委員会"],["majority","過半数"]]},{"t":"Muji's president apologizes; no date to restart its online store; leaks at the Cabinet Office and a securities firm too","x":"On the afternoon of the 12th, the president of Ryohin Keikaku, which runs Muji, apologized at a press conference. Up to 27.26 million records of app members may have leaked. About the online store, stopped since the 6th, he said safety comes first and he cannot say when it will reopen (Senken Shimbun, Kyodo). New: About 63,000 email addresses leaked from the Cabinet Office's email newsletter because of unauthorized access to Arara, the company that sent the emails (Nikkei, NHK, Kyodo). New: At SMBC Nikko Securities, data on up to 56,487 people, including stock balances, may have leaked from its employee stock system (Jiji, Nikkei, Business+IT). New: About 14,500 records from the Yasukuni Shrine website too (ITmedia only). New at night: Tochigi Prefecture's local products shopping site \"Gurutochi\" was also attacked and changed to send visitors to a fake site, and the prefecture is warning people (Shimotsuke Shimbun, NHK).","w":[["apologize","おわびする"],["leak","漏れる"]]},{"t":"Bird flu in Kyoto, the first at a Japanese poultry farm this autumn; flu also spreads in Tohoku","x":"New: Bird flu was confirmed at a poultry farm in Kameoka, Kyoto Prefecture, the first at a farm in Japan this autumn. About 200,000 birds will be killed. The prefecture says infected chicken and eggs will not be sold in stores (Yomiuri TV, ABC, Nikkei, ANN). New: Influenza is spreading in Tohoku too. In Yamagata, all health centers are at the warning level (YBC only), and in Fukushima classes were closed at 42 schools (Fukushima Minyu only). New: After a fire in Fukuyama, Hiroshima, in which three people died, the eldest son who lived with them was arrested on suspicion of arson (NHK only). New: This morning, some places in Kanto and Tokai had the coldest morning of the autumn, but it will be sunny and warmer in the daytime (tenki.jp, Weathernews). New: In Sendai, a bus braked suddenly and seven passengers were hurt (Kahoku Shimpo, NHK, tbc). The first trial of Watanabe, a leader of the \"Luffy\" group, began, and he partly denied the robbery-death charge (Kyodo, Jiji, Mainichi). New: A former accountant was arrested on suspicion of stealing more than 2.1 billion yen from his company (Jiji, Mainichi, ANN).","w":[["bird flu","鳥インフルエンザ"],["poultry farm","養鶏場"]]},{"t":"The EU plans a law to ban \"tricky screens\" online; Australia's leader criticized at COP31","x":"New: Australian Prime Minister Albanese was criticized for not mentioning coal or gas in his speech at COP31 (SBS, ABC). New: South Korean President Lee Jae-myung will go to the ASEAN meeting in the Philippines and the APEC meeting in China next week (Korea Times only). New: The EU announced a bill to ban \"dark patterns\" online and to require a check before a free trial changes to a paid subscription. Companies that break the rules could be fined up to 6% of their sales. This also affects Japanese app and game companies (Kyodo, Nikkei, Yomiuri). Japan's Fair Trade Commission accepted Amazon's plan to stop requiring prices to be lower than on other sites (Kyodo, Jiji, Yomiuri, NHK). In the US Senate election in Mississippi, Democrat Collum beat the Republican senator (CNBC, Al Jazeera, NPR, BBC). Schools in Italy, the UK and Ireland received false bomb threat emails, and at least 300 schools in Italy were evacuated (CNN, Reuters, CBS, NHK). New: In Chile, truck drivers went on a national strike against higher fuel prices, affecting deliveries (El Mercurio, The Clinic, teleSUR).","w":[["subscription","サブスク(定期購入)"],["ban","禁止する"]]},{"t":"Up to 980,000 people's data may have leaked from the Japan Chamber of Commerce's online tests; Soft99 and Edion too","x":"There was unauthorized access to the online tests, such as bookkeeping, run by the Japan Chamber of Commerce and Industry. Names, results and scores of up to about 980,000 people who took tests since April 2022 may have leaked (ITmedia, Kyodo, ANN). New: At Toyama Prefectural University, email addresses of about 3,000 students and staff leaked (NHK, Hokkoku, Kitanihon Shimbun). New: The online shop of Soft99, a maker of car care goods, was attacked, and personal data of up to about 137,000 people, including card data, may have leaked (NHK, Nikkei). New: Australia will create an office to watch AI safety after OpenAI's AI got into a government website (AP, The Next Web). At furniture maker Nitori, up to 37.62 million records (Kyodo, Nikkei, NHK). New: A bad program was put into the online shop of electronics store Edion, and over 500 records including card data may have leaked (NHK, Kansai TV, ABC). New: Sumitomo Life's health service \"Vitality\" was also affected through its contractor NTT Data, about 80,000 people (ITmedia, Nikkei, ABC). New: Sapporo's transit guide \"Sapporo Eki Bus Navi\" was attacked, and false information such as subway suspensions was sent out (HBC, UHB, HTB).","w":[["unauthorized access","不正アクセス"],["personal data","個人情報"]]},{"t":"National health insurance cap to rise by 30,000 yen to 960,000 yen; maglev's Nagoya station delayed to 2033 or later","x":"New: The yearly cap on national health insurance premiums will rise by 30,000 yen to 960,000 yen in fiscal 2027. It is for people with high incomes (Kyodo, Nikkei). New: SoftBank Group had a loss of 768 billion yen for April to September, with a big loss from changing its US data center plans (on the 10th; Jiji, Kyodo, NHK). China said it will extend for two more months the stop of its extra 24% tariff on goods from the US (Jiji, Reuters). Russia put all of Japan Tobacco's local companies under temporary control (Reuters, Kabutan, Nikkei). New: The Nagoya station of the Chuo Shinkansen maglev line will be finished in 2033 or later. JR Central says this will not change when the Shinagawa-Nagoya line opens (Nikkei, Kyodo, Chunichi). New: JR East will bring \"walk-through gates\" that you can pass without touching your phone to about 40 stations, including all Yamanote Line stations, in spring 2028 (NHK, TBS, CNET).","w":[["insurance","保険"],["cap","上限"]]},{"t":"Asia pro baseball: Samurai Japan beats Taiwan; Australia edges South Korea","x":"New: In the Asia professional baseball championship, Australia narrowly beat South Korea (NTV, Nikkan, Daily). New: On day 5 of the Kyushu sumo tournament, yokozuna Hoshoryu lost for the third time in a row (NHK only). On the night of the 12th, the Asia Professional Baseball Championship began, and Samurai Japan beat Taiwan 5-0. Masaki hit home runs in two at-bats in a row, and pitcher Kanemaru gave up no runs in seven innings (Chunichi Sports, Hochi, Daily). New: Major League's Cy Young Awards went to Schlittler of the Yankees in the AL and Misiorowski of the Brewers in the NL, both with all first-place votes (MLB, CBS). New: On day 4 of the sumo tournament, Atamifuji won his fourth straight and leads alone (NHK, Sponichi). Japan's national soccer team will play Brazil in Singapore on the 14th (FIFA, Football Channel). New: Ten players applied for free agency in pro baseball, the most in 15 years (Jiji, Sponichi). Ohtani's NL MVP will be announced on the morning of the 13th. New: In the NBA, Rui Hachimura scored 13 points, but the Clippers lost big to the Suns (Kyodo, NHK, Basketball King).","w":[["edge","僅差で勝つ"],["home run","ホームラン"]]}],"ex":{"saudi":"In the Middle East, an armed group and Saudi Arabia keep fighting, and oil prices are rising. This connects to gas prices in Japan.","tax":"A plan to lower the tax on food you buy at the supermarket from 8% to 1%. It passed the House of Representatives, and debate in the House of Councillors started on the 11th. It is not decided yet.","cyber":"Bad actors keep breaking into the computers of companies and government offices and stealing information such as names and addresses. On November 6, the government made an emergency package and will spend about 10 billion yen.","mmx":"A Japanese probe has left for Mars. The plan is to bring back sand from a small moon near Mars.","sato":"The Hanshin Tigers agreed to let Sato, this year's \"Triple Crown\" hitter, try to play in Major League Baseball in America.","series":"SoftBank beat DeNA 4 games in a row and became Japan's champion for the second year in a row (10/28).","yokohama":"There was an election to choose the leader (mayor) of Yokohama, and a new person was chosen.","past":"Three weeks of worries about a big typhoon and a volcano, a new governor of Okinawa and new ministers, and higher interest rates in America.","ukr":"Talks to end the war between Russia and Ukraine were held in Abu Dhabi on November 10 and 11. A large prisoner exchange was reportedly agreed, but there was no big progress such as a ceasefire. The US envoy plans to meet President Putin in Moscow next.","typhoon":"Typhoon No. 30 changed into an extratropical low on the night of the 25th. On the 26th, heavy rain is possible from Kyushu to Kanto.","shogi":"Shogi player Tomoka Nishiyama decided to become a \"kishi,\" the professional player status open to both men and women. In April next year she will be the first woman kishi in shogi history.","reporter":"A Japanese newspaper reporter was arrested in Russia as a \"spy.\" The Japanese government says he is not a spy and asks Russia to send him home soon.","hamaoka":"Local residents went to court asking to stop the Hamaoka nuclear plant in Shizuoka, but the court dismissed the case. On November 5, the residents appealed.","israel":"There was a parliament election in Israel, and the prime minister's side may not win more than half of the seats.","teisu":"Political parties are talking about whether to reduce the number of members of the House of Representatives.","fed":"US consumer prices in October rose more than expected, and more people now think America's central bank (the Fed) will raise interest rates in December.","cold":"After Ritto (November 7), it is getting colder. Hokkaido dropped below minus 10°C, and Tokyo had its coldest morning this autumn.","typhoon31":"A strong typhoon will come closest to the Ogasawara Islands, south of Tokyo, around the morning of the 5th. It will not reach the main islands, but Kanto should watch out for heavy rain.","midterm":"In America, there was an election for members of Congress. The opposition Democrats will have more seats in both the House and the Senate. It will be harder for the president's policies to pass, and it affected the yen and stocks.","tokai":"A strong earthquake hit the Tokai area in the middle of the night on November 8. Aichi Prefecture had shindo 5+ for the first time in about 30 years, and some people were injured."}};
